      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“When morning paints the eastern sky,” by Cordelia Moïse Cohen (1809-1869), first published in 1842, appears under the subject “Immortality of the Soul” as Hymn 54 in <tei:hi rend="italic">Hymns Written for the Service of the Hebrew Congregation Beth Elohim, South Carolina</tei:hi> (Penina Moïse et al., Ḳ.Ḳ. Beth Elohim, 1842), p. 57. That page is missing in the one copy of the first edition we know to exist. Thankfully, the hymn appears under the same subject as Hymn 40 in <tei:hi rend="italic">Hymns Written for the Use of Hebrew Congregations</tei:hi> (Penina Moïse et al., Ḳ.Ḳ. Beth Elohim, 1856), p. 44. –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_39546_notes"/>
